        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(sdk): preserve zero event id components",
        "body": "Closes #101768\n\nAI-assisted: drafted and validated by Codex. I understand the change: it preserves protocol-valid zero values when the SDK builds normalized event ids.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where SDK consumers could receive normalized gateway event ids that silently dropped valid `seq: 0` and `ts: 0` components, weakening replay/live dedupe identity for zero-sequence gateway events.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe gateway protocol allows event sequence values starting at zero, but `normalizeGatewayEvent()` built ids with a truthy filter. This change filters out only absent optional parts, so numeric zero values remain part of the stable SDK event id.\n\n## User Impact\n\nSDK consumers now get stable normalized ids for the first gateway event in a stream, avoiding avoidable replay or dedupe confusion around valid zero-valued sequence and timestamp fields.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Focused proof passed: `/Users/harjothk/.cache/codex-runtimes/codex-primary-runtime/dependencies/node/bin/node scripts/run-vitest.mjs packages/sdk/src/normalize.test.ts -- --reporter=verbose` (1 file, 5 tests).\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- Autoreview passed clean: `/Users/harjothk/.cache/codex-runtimes/codex-primary-runtime/dependencies/python/bin/python3 .agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local`.\n",
